  "content": {
    "title": "Confirmed: 'Virgin River' Season 8 Production Starts April 2026",
    "text": "Since its debut, every season of the beloved small-town drama has landed in Netflix’s Top 10—often holding the No. 1 spot for weeks at a time. With Virgin River season 7 premiering on March 12, 2026, Netflix has already confirmed the story isn’t ending anytime soon. In fact, the streamer renewed the series for Season 8 back in July 2025, well ahead of the latest premiere.Here’s everything we know so far about Virgin River Season 8, including who’s expected to return and which characters are—and aren't—returning.🎬 SIGN UP for Parade’s Daily newsletter to get the latest pop culture news & celebrity interviews delivered right to your inbox 🎬 Martin Henderson, Alexandra Breckenridge in 'Virgin River'Courtesy of Netflix (Courtesy of Netflix)When will 'Virgin River' season 8 start filming?Per Deadline, production on Season 8 of Virgin River is slated to begin production on April 22, 2026. Production will run through August.Related: ‘Virgin River’ Season 8 Shocker: Who’s Staying and Who’s Leaving?When will Season 8 of 'Virgin River' premiere?Netflix has yet to announce an official premiere date for Season 8 of Virgin River, but check back here for updates.Season 8 of Virgin River will pick up approximately four months after the events of the Season 7 finale.Colin Lawrence, Kandyse McClureNetflxi (Netflxi)What cast is returning for Season 8 of 'Virgin River'?Alexandra Breckenridge as Melinda \"Mel\" MonroeMartin Henderson as Jack SheridanTim Matheson as Dr. Vernon MullinsAnnette O'Toole as Hope McCreaBen Hollingsworth as Dan BradyZibby Allen as Brie SheridanSarah Dugdale as LizzieKai Bradbury as Denny CutlerColin Lawrence as John \"Preacher\" MiddletonKandyse McClure as Kaia BryantJohn Allen Nelson as Everett ReidTeryl Rothery as Muriel Saint ClaireWho is not returning for Season 8 of 'Virgin River'?According to Deadline, we know of at least two characters that will not be returning for Season 8 of Virgin River: Charmaine (Lauren Hammersley) and Det. Mike Valenzuela (Marco Grazzini). Read on for more about these characters.Lauren Hammersley as Charmaine RobertsIn Season 7, Charmaine was kidnapped by her Grant (Alessandro Juliani), the owner of the salon where she worked. Grant was obsessed with Charmaine and killed Calvin (David Cubitt). He kidnapped Charmaine and the twins and held them captive until Brie (Zibby Allen) and Mike (Marco Grazzini) were able to rescue her.Marco Grazzini as Det. Mike ValenzuelaMike was a former Marine who served with Jack and Brady and is currently an LAPD detective. The character joined in Season 2 and exited in Season 7 as a series regular.David Cubitt/Josh Blacker as CalvinCalvin was the de facto villain in the series. He was introduced in the first season as the leader of an illegal marijuana operation in the forest with Jimmy (Ian Tracey) as his right-hand man. Calvin was revealed to be the baby daddy of Charmaine's twins in Season 5. Cubitt originated the role with Blacker taking over in Season 6.Mark Ghanimé as Dr. Cameron HayekGhanimé's Dr. Hayek had a reduced role in Season 6 after he reconciled with his ex. The character did not appear at all in Season 7.Sara Canning as VictoriaVictoria was a medical investigator in town to investigate Doc Mullins. She was a former colleague of Mike (Marco Grazzini) and finally admitted she had a crush on him back during their cop days. While Canning only had a guest starring role on the series, if Grazzini's Det. Mike is written back in after Season 8, there's a possibility for a new romance storyline for Mike and Victoria.Rachel Drance as MarleyMarley was the birth mother of Mel and Jack's new baby. Drance had a recurring guest star role as Marley in Seasons 7 and 8. While it has been confirmed that Hammersley and Grazzini won't appear in Season 8, that doesn't mean they and Ghanimé won't return in future seasons.Who's new to the cast of Virgin River in Season 8?Cody Kearsley as ClayKearsley joined in a recurring role in Season 8 as Jack's new ranch hand, Clay. He'll guest star again through the upcoming season as Clay continues to search for his missing sister.Matty Finnochio as TonyFinnochio will recur in a guest starring role as Tony Hope's temporary assistant while Lizzie (Sarah Dugdale) is on maternity leave.Austin Nichols as EliEli is the pediatric cardiothoracic surgeon working on Mel's baby. He also has a complicated professional and romantic past with Mel.What will happen in Virgin River Season 8?At the end of Season 7, Mel escorted her newborn son to the NICU and was able to say the words she's been wanting to say for years, \"I'm his mother. Breckenridge, who plays Mel in the series, has been waiting for Season 8’s storyline for a long time. “I am excited to see Mel as a mother,” she tells Netflix's Tudum. “I think we’ve anticipated that moment for far too long. It should be sweet. I’m sure it’ll be harder than she thinks it’s going to be.” Season 8 will focus on the challenges of raising a child with special needs and the strain it puts on parents and their marriage.Showrunner Patrick Sean Smith told Deadline that Season 8 will also focus on Denny \"going through the application process and interviews\" for medical school. Smith also said Muriel (Teryl Rothery) will enter a new romance with someone “who might be a little close to Mel,” confirming that it’s Everett (John Allen Nelson)!Smith also said the upcoming season will find Jack working on getting the farm running as well as further exploring themes of sacrifice, rebirth, and feeling haunted by the past.Next, The Heroic Dog Behind a Real Kentucky Law Is Getting a Movie Starring Trevor DonovanThis story was originally published by Parade on Mar 16, 2026, where it first appeared in the TV section. Add Parade as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
